WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.660
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.660
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.930
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.930
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.730
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.730
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.900
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.900
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.860
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.860
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.870
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.870
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.920
Keep your eyes on me, okay!?

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.920
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.790
Attention please, attention please.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:54.460
We're gonna arrive at the
John F. Kennedy airport very soon.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.900
Sana-chan.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:10.770
We're here.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.360
Nao, wake up.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.280
Sana-chan.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.490
We made it to New York, huh?

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.120
Do your best, okay?

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:30.790
Yeah.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.960
New York...

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.470
New York...

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:45.970
Suspense in New York

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.770
My name is Sana Kurata!

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.890
Thank you, you're welcome!

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:52.770
I'm from Tokyo.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.690
Welcome to America.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:55.980
You can go through.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.570
I'm in New York.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:00.490
I'm feeling at my best right now.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:07.870
I finally got  a sound out of it.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.370
We're already in New York?

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.290
I'm about to faint.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:18.880
I want to see New York

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.960
Actually I was already here a couple of times.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.840
Welcome to America,
are you visiting?

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:18.840
I suppose so.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.880
Right now we're over here right?

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.390
Is this Manhattan?

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.100
I don't know Broadway,
what kind of place is it?

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.270
The guidebook says it takes an hour to get there by taxi.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:31.390
Where's Gary Hamilton's house that we're supposed to go to?

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.560
They're supposed to be somewhere to pick us up.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.280
The guidebook says if you're not careful in New York all your luggage will be stolen.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.780
So be careful everyone.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.860
If a girl goes out at night alone in New York, there's definitely going to be danger.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:43.570
Don't ever leave, Sana-chan!

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:44.570
Ok!

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:45.990
The guidebook says...

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:51.580
The flight from Japan to the JFK airport doesn't have an evening flight.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.460
You could take a taxi but it doesn't look like you will.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.510
What? What's going on?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.470
Alright! With this trumpet I will...

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.890
You are Kamura Naozumi, right?

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.690
And you are Kurata Sana, right?

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:14.770
Yes, yes, yes.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:17.060
Put away your trumpet now.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:19.980
Ah, then you're the producer, right?

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.570
Mr. Gary Hamilton?

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:25.570
I'm the housekeeper,
Alfred Mackvakiavan.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:27.280
I'm here to pick you up.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.790
Mr. Housekeeper?

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:29.990
Mr. Mackvakiavan?

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:33.080
You must be really tired coming from so far away.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:37.880
Please come with me. I will take you to Mr. Hamilton's house.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.380
Pleased to meet you.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.090
Pleased...

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:43.760
These are our bodyguards.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:44.760
Let's go.{guesslation}

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:45.970
Loop!

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.980
Is that Manhattan? Is that the Empire State building?

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.560
Is that the Statue of Liberty?

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.900
New York! Rei-kun, did you see?

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.270
I can't move, Sana-chan.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:04:59.570
Maeda-san, take a look!

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.070
I can't move, Nao.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.990
Brooklyn! Brooklyn! Manhattan!

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.280
Loop, loop!

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.870
You're too close to the camera.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.870
I'm not telling you where they flew to

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.580
That's a huge house!

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:15.290
Sana-chan...

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:17.790
That's the president's White House, isn't it?

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.460
No, that's our house.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:22.670
White House isn't in New York.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.970
It's in Washington DC.

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:30.760
Please come this way.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:37.520
A party!

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.270
Could this possibly be...

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.190
A welcoming party for us?

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:42.480
Yeah, surely!

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.280
Actually no.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.860
This is our weekly ball.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.200
Oh after all..

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.660
Come this way please.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:53.080
Madame.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:56.160
We already brought them here.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.370
I see.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.380
I'm Kurata Sana.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:03.090
I'm Kamura Naozumi.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.680
I'm Kurata's manager, Sagami Rei.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:08.760
Kamura's manager...

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.390
- Mysterious white Bat...
- Babbit!

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.470
I'm the German born American Babbit.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.940
What's with her attitude?

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:19.440
It's hard to describe.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.230
Oh maybe because we don't speak the same language.

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:23.360
Maybe so.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.280
Why don't we use the language of music instead.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:28.110
Let me try too.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:34.040
I'm here, I'm here, Kurata Sana from Japan is here.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:40.460
Direct flight across the ocean with Naozumi-kun.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:44.460
Invited here by the famous producer Mr. Hamilton.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.590
Alright, Naozumi-kun solo!

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:52.680
Invited to America, fly fly fly, fly here.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.100
Babin babon.

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.350
You understand now, right?

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.190
Come on?

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.110
So it's like that.

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.150
Please enjoy yourself.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.240
What about Mr. Hamilton?

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.870
We'll take care of your rooms.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.080
Please enjoy the party.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:20.750
Ok.

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.880
I guess you're supposed to feel like that when you're enjoying a party.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:27.090
Party Party

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.800
Oh this is American Style,
it is a bit different.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.300
How do you do?

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.380
Hello everyone, I'm Kurata Sana.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.590
Alright, Naozumi-kun.

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.090
Good evening, everyone.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:35.680
I'm Kamura Naozumi, from Japan.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.060
Your eyes are blue, are you half?

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.060
That's right.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.560
What were you talking about with Michelle?

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.270
Yeah, it really makes one suspicious.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:44.690
Oh Michelle?

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:47.690
Mr. Hamilton's wife's name is Michelle?

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.360
Yeah, I thought I heard that name before.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:52.570
You guys don't know
who you were talking to?

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:58.370
The guidebook says Michelle Hamilton was a famous Broadway costume designer.

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:01.660
But this book says she's the queen of Broadway.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:04.460
So she's really great, isn't she?

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.380
What was that now?

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.590
Sana-chan..?

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:12.970
Sana-chan?

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:15.090
New York is cold, isn't it?

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.510
Let's find something hot to drink.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:30.280
Sana-chan!

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:49.300
Hayama...

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:53.800
Hayama? Who's that?
Your boyfriend?

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:57.470
Do we look alike? Don't be joking.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:02.560
I'm Brad. I've never left New York since I was born, Kurata.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:05.480
Of course I never went to Japan or any other foreign country.

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:07.190
It's nice to meet you.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.690
Sana-chan, what just happened now?

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:11.690
Ahh! Hayama-kun!

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:15.700
Oh Kamura! I don't want to have to explain to you!

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:18.370
Ok then, let Babbit explain everything.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:39.510
Hayama                            Brad

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:22.080
Hayama and Brad look the same, but their eyes are different.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.500
Their personalities aren't the same either.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:27.170
If he were Hayama, "Akito, do you like sushi?", "I don't hate it."

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:30.460
If he were Brad, "Brad, do you like sushi?"

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:35.880
"Oh yes! I love sushi!" "Very very lovely yum yum!"

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.090
You're horrible!

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:39.180
Oh I'm just a little embarrassed right now.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.100
Brad?

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:43.560
Yeah, I know everything about this house.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.480
If you have anything you don't understand, ask Mr. Brad here.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:47.480
Ok, come with me.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:48.560
Coming...

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.570
This is the kitchen.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:54.860
Actually you don't have to tell us where the kitchen is.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.200
Listen carefully.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:59.070
Even at the party we're all rivals.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:02.280
One's survival in the party world is always very uncertain.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.660
Even if you beat your partner.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.580
You have to try to find a way to protect your own status.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:07.160
If you don't eat someone else, you'll be eaten.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.380
There's usually sausages in there.

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:10.580
Alright, next.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:12.460
This is the training room.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:14.380
Kurata is 13, right?

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.090
Why do you look like a little kid?

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.880
What the hell are you doing?!

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.390
Do you wanna fight, Kamura?

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:22.180
Do people with your appearance always do stuff like this?

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:27.480
Using the equipment here can allow one to get a good figure for the dance floor.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:31.060
The actresses and the models at the party are at least teenagers.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:32.690
Everyone's exercising.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:33.860
Alright, next room.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:37.070
You two look good together.
You're lovers?

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.570
You're not lovers?

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:41.450
- Just good friends.
- Yeah.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.580
Huh, what was that?

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:47.160
Starting from here only the servants are allowed to enter.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.750
So next is the garden.

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.670
Previously it wasn't Babbit.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:51.130
What did you see?

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.590
This is the end of the garden.

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:54.800
This fast? Why is it like this?

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:59.590
Because Broadway is a very crowded place, you should go back early.

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:01.590
But we've been invited here.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.970
I just want to be friendly, that's all.

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.390
See you, goodnight.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.270
What's with him?

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:10.850
Sana-chan, I found you!

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.980
Ah your rooms are ready!

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.070
It's very luxurious.

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:19.280
You two are so naive.

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:21.700
Oh geez, Maeda-san.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:23.200
Let's go, Sana-chan.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:24.280
Ok.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.380
Ready?

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:39.670
From here on are Maeda-sama, Sagami-sama, and Kamura-sama's rooms.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.590
I'm taking a leave.

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:43.840
Um what about Mr. Hamilton...

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:46.720
Goodnight then.

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.390
Let's just go rest.

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:53.400
Nao, Sana-chan, goodnight.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.900
Goodnight!

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.360
Oh well, can't help it.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:59.070
Goodnight, Sana-chan. Naozumi-kun.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:00.610
Goodnight!

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:02.860
Alright then me too, goodnight.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.030
Goodnight.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:06.490
Miss, come this way.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:08.740
Sana-chan!

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:09.700
Hmm?

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.370
Tomorrow we'll do our best, ok?

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.670
Goodnight!

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:16.540
Goodnight, Naozumi-kun.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.880
Do you need your luggage carried over?

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:23.840
No, just leave it there.
Thank you, Shimura-san.

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.430
It's Ramsy.

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.390
Ah, I'm sorry!

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:31.230
Because in my family we have a servant and her name is Shimura-san.

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:32.850
She's as sweet as you.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:37.770
You seem to have a very good relationship with the person in the next room.

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:39.820
Yes! Friend, friend!

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:41.690
Actually in this room...

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.200
Ah, it's nothing.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:46.280
Excuse me.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:49.490
What was that?

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:50.580
Biron!

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:53.710
How strange this house seems.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.250
Asako...

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:28.570
Usiarumo what is it?

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.580
{parte b}

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:34.080
It's Omuraisu (Omelette Rice)!

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.580
Sana-chan's drawing zone. Prepare paper and crayon.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.590
First you draw one mountain...

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.800
...then comes the water...

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.760
...there goes 2 cups...

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:46.880
...plus 2 earlobes...

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.890
...butterfly, butterfly... fly over here...

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:50.890
...aha you have a tail...

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:53.060
...drawing on the left, drawing on the right...

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.980
...draw the arrow shaped eye...

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:57.060
...and then another arrow for the other eye...

00:13:57.060 --> 00:14:01.070
...two people jump over a wooden horse...

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:03.360
...Ku Ku Ku shapes...

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:05.280
...plus 6 eyes...

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:07.280
...and she's complete!

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.780
Jump, jump... hey hey hey!

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:12.580
This is my picture!

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.500
What?

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.510
Maybe I was just dreaming.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:33.680
Ahh! Help me!

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:37.180
Sana-chan!

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:46.280
Sana-chan! What's wrong?

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.280
Are you alright?

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.150
Sana-chan!

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:50.950
What happened?

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.570
I'm confused.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:55.580
I suddenly couldn't raise this barbell.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:58.410
How much does the barbell weigh?

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:01.380
20 Kg, it should be easy to lift up.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:05.800
But why did you decide to lift weights and exercise so early in the morning?

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:07.130
That's because...

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.260
What?

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:09.630
To build my figure.

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:11.010
Did you say 20 Kg?

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:13.680
This barbell is 50 Kg.

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:16.430
You can't do 50 Kg, Sana-chan.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:18.270
That's really too heavy.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.890
But I originally was going to get a 20 Kg one.

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.980
It was 20 Kg in the beginning.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:24.150
What?

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:26.690
Each ring is 10, so it adds up to 20.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:29.570
The outer was 15 each which adds up to 30.

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:30.990
With a total of 50 Kg.

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:35.080
But I really only intended to add 10 Kg each time.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.870
Sana-chan, pounds and kilograms aren't the same.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.250
What's that?

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:40.660
Let me explain to you.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:16:05.400
Pounds

00:15:40.960 --> 00:16:05.400
Kilograms

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.580
Look here because Rei-kun's explanation wasn't too clear.

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:45.290
So let Babbit explain to you exclusively.

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:49.590
In America, the unit of measurement more frequently used is the pound not the kilogram.

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:53.760
Here look, 1 Pound equal .454 Kg

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:58.390
So Sana-chan thought that 10Kg = 10 Lbs.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:01.270
But really 10 Lbs. is 4.54 Kg.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.980
No, Rei-kun, it was already 10 pounds less.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.900
Are you saying that someone added weights?

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:12.860
Yeah, even though this is the only explanation, we don't have any proof.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:16.580
Even I don't know when the weights were added.

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:18.240
Maybe it's the time difference.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:19.540
Maybe it's him.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:20.540
Brad?

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:23.290
No, I really don't know what's going on.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:24.960
Maybe I turned stupid.

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:32.090
It was a hard chance for us to get into New York.

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:34.430
So we have to stand on the Broadway stage!

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:38.010
Right?

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:39.260
Yeah.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:40.560
See see, I knew it.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:44.770
Broadway dance dance win!

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:49.570
I'm going to do that too! I did it!

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:51.360
Look, Sana-chan! Look, look!

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:02.660
What's that truck trying to do?

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:03.790
This way, Sana-chan!

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.460
What the hell are you doing?!

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:10.840
You bastard!

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:11.920
Good morning.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.720
Kurata, Kamura, did you have a good night's sleep?

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:17.760
What's wrong, did something happen?

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:19.600
You seem to be very calm.

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:22.470
Look at that, we were almost hit.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:24.980
You were targeted?

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:28.560
Like I said, going back real quick is probably better.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:32.650
To be invited here means you'll definitely be targeted.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.110
What is with him...?

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:42.410
Be careful, Sana-chan.

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:43.660
Don't worry.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:47.670
There's not gonna be a crazy car, or a crazy horse after you enter the house.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:51.000
Here in America you don't know what can happen.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.340
Maybe there will be a really mean old man.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.090
But we'll talk about it when the time comes.

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:55.970
Sana-chan, stop!

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:59.180
Time for pictures, don't move!

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.220
Can Babbit be in the picture too?

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.220
Come on, smile!

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:02.390
Sana-chan! Naozumi-kun!

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.690
Ah... it's alright, it's alright.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:11.570
This week's Sana-chan and Naozumi-kun!

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:13.280
That's dangerous!

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:15.360
Oh are you ok?

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:16.780
Was it you?

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:18.860
How could it be?

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:29.370
Eating American food in such a big dining room makes me feel a lot better.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:32.090
How dare you say that after hiding in the corner eating.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:34.960
Are we really being targeted?

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.380
We can only assume that.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:40.260
Eating big spoonfuls of Cornflake Paste really adds a lot of American Flavor to food, Sana-chan.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:41.260
What should we do?

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:42.600
Babbit's going to the other side.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:44.260
I don't know who would do this.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:47.770
Sana-chan, you're not gonna eat this?

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:50.560
Maeda-san!

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:54.190
Sana-chan has been practicing since morning. I was just trying to help her out.

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:55.780
You're acting like a child, Maeda-san.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:59.280
You should say it tastes really good, right?

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:01.570
You'll be kicked out like this.

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:04.870
Do you have to be like this?

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:08.500
This isn't good, Maeda-san.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:11.580
Maeda-san?

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:14.380
I feel sick...

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:15.300
Maeda-san!

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:16.590
Rei-kun, call an ambulance!

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:17.170
Ok!

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:21.130
Who's behind this?

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:18.380
I'm worried.

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:20.760
Next is a car in America.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:27.180
How can this happen?!

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:31.270
If Maeda-san didn't eat it, it would have been Sana-chan!

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:34.060
Sana-chan, Maeda-san will be alright.

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:37.780
Even though he looks really skinny, he's actually very healthy.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.490
Excuse me.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.070
We're really sorry.

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:46.790
If I had checked everything carefully this wouldn't have happened.

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:48.500
Ramsy-san, no!

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:51.870
Actually yesterday weren't you going to tell me something?

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:54.790
You said "this room... "
What were you going to say?

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:58.800
I'm really sorry, I can't say anything.

00:19:58.800 --> 00:19:59.760
Why?!

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:01.170
I'm really sorry!

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:02.180
Ramsy-san.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:06.180
Excuse me.

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:07.600
Mackbeagongon-san.

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:09.270
It's Mackvakiavan.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:10.680
Excuse me.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:13.980
I just got back from the hospital.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:16.190
Maeda-san is not in a life threatening condition.

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:18.070
What a relief.

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:20.990
But the cause is still under investigation.

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:24.780
Before the investigation results come out, you should be patient for a while.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:27.080
Sana-chan, it's him.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:30.500
Didn't he tell us yesterday where the sausages are being kept?

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:32.410
I don't know if he has anything to do with this.

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:36.670
You mean... he's accepting responsibility for being a criminal?

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:39.880
Yeah, that part sounds weird too.

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:45.470
Then, please excuse me.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:50.060
Sana-chan, Naozumi-kun.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.770
After coming here, I've noticed too many strange things happening.

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:55.480
It's better that we don't attract attention.

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:57.690
If something happens to you...

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:59.070
...no that can't happen.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:03.780
Anyway I think when Mr. Gary Hamilton comes back everything will be cleared.

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:06.200
Until then, we'll have to protect ourselves.

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:07.820
Yes.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.120
That's right.

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:12.080
Oh oh oh! Night comes down.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:15.120
